[info] >  PitchLab: Raw request data: {"idea":"MoorSafe is a premium, solar-powered, low-voltage pest deterrent device that mounts onto mooring ropes to prevent rodents and insects from boarding vessels. It combines an electrified deterrent surface with a durable marine-grade housing. The goal is a “set-and-forget” solution for boat owners and marinas.\n","category":"Hardware","problem":"Rodents and pests commonly use mooring ropes to access boats, causing damage, contamination, and safety concerns. Existing solutions like plastic guards or makeshift barriers are unreliable, unattractive, and require frequent maintenance. There is no effective, automated solution currently on the market.\n","targetMarket":"The target market includes recreational boat owners, marinas, and commercial vessel operators in New Zealand, Australia, and globally. These users already spend heavily on maintenance and protection, indicating willingness to pay for a reliable solution. MoorSafe can be positioned as a premium marine accessory with global scalability.\n","experience":"The founder has strong financial, commercial, and project management experience, with exposure to construction, logistics, and product development. There is also direct access to marine industry insights through family experience. However, technical engineering and hardware manufacturing expertise will require external partners.\n","capacity":"Current capacity is limited due to multiple business commitments, but sufficient to drive early-stage MVP development and validation. External partners such as design firms and manufacturers will be leveraged for technical execution. Time and focus will need to increase if the product gains traction.\n","budget":"The MVP can be developed very cheaply using 3D printing and off-the-shelf components, with an initial budget of approximately $500–$1,000. This allows for rapid prototyping and testing without significant financial risk. Further development stages may require $10k–$50k depending on complexity and production readiness.\n","network":"The founder has access to a strong network across construction, transport, and Pacific business communities, as well as potential marine users for testing. Early engagement with design firms and manufacturers is already underway. Additional connections in marine retail, distribution, and engineering will strengthen the pathway to market.\n"} {"user":"PitchLab: Raw request data: {\"idea\":\"MoorSafe is a premium, solar-powered, low-voltage pest deterrent device that mounts onto mooring ropes to prevent rodents and insects from boarding vessels. It combines an electrified deterrent surface with a durable marine-grade housing. The goal is a “set-and-forget” solution for boat owners and marinas.\\n\",\"category\":\"Hardware\",\"problem\":\"Rodents and pests commonly use mooring ropes to access boats, causing damage, contamination, and safety concerns. Existing solutions like plastic guards or makeshift barriers are unreliable, unattractive, and require frequent maintenance. There is no effective, automated solution currently on the market.\\n\",\"targetMarket\":\"The target market includes recreational boat owners, marinas, and commercial vessel operators in New Zealand, Australia, and globally. These users already spend heavily on maintenance and protection, indicating willingness to pay for a reliable solution. MoorSafe can be positioned as a premium marine accessory with global scalability.\\n\",\"experience\":\"The founder has strong financial, commercial, and project management experience, with exposure to construction, logistics, and product development. There is also direct access to marine industry insights through family experience. However, technical engineering and hardware manufacturing expertise will require external partners.\\n\",\"capacity\":\"Current capacity is limited due to multiple business commitments, but sufficient to drive early-stage MVP development and validation. External partne