[info] >  PitchLab: Raw request data: {"idea":"Uber competitor business model where drivers only pay a fixed monthly fee - drivers will keep 100% of the fares earned.\n","category":"SaaS","problem":"\"Drivers feel punished by commission-based platforms\nOn Uber-style models, the platform takes a cut of every trip, so drivers can feel like they are doing the work while the platform keeps too much of the upside. Your model gives drivers 100% of each fare, which is much easier to understand and feels fairer.\nDrivers want predictable costs\nA fixed monthly subscription turns platform cost into a known business expense. That solves the frustration of variable commissions eating into income, especially during high-demand weeks when drivers are working hardest.\nDrivers are losing too much of their income to commission-based platforms and need a fairer, more predictable pricing model that lets them keep 100% of what they earn.\"\n","targetMarket":"Target market: Uber drivers, rideshare drivers, and traditional cab drivers who are tired of losing a percentage of every fare. The MVP gives them a simple alternative: pay one fixed monthly fee, keep 100% of fares, and operate with more control, predictability, and better earning potential.\n","experience":"Relevant experience: 20+ years in finance, accounting, forecasting, business partnering, and growth planning, plus hands-on experience building and evaluating multiple ventures across construction, transport, tourism, consulting, and tech. You also understand SME pain points, pricing models, compliance, and how to turn ideas into practical MVPs.\n","capacity":"5-10 hours a week whilst working on all my other projects.\n","budget":"Total is probably NZ$5000 max.\n","network":"Strong business network across New Zealand and Samoa through accounting, consulting, transport, construction, tourism, and community work. Access to SME owners, potential pilot customers, business advisers, and referral channels, plus growing links to investors, grant bodies, and strategic partners relevant to early validation.\n"} {"user":"PitchLab: Raw request data: {\"idea\":\"Uber competitor business model where drivers only pay a fixed monthly fee - drivers will keep 100% of the fares earned.\\n\",\"category\":\"SaaS\",\"problem\":\"\\\"Drivers feel punished by commission-based platforms\\nOn Uber-style models, the platform takes a cut of every trip, so drivers can feel like they are doing the work while the platform keeps too much of the upside. Your model gives drivers 100% of each fare, which is much easier to understand and feels fairer.\\nDrivers want predictable costs\\nA fixed monthly subscription turns platform cost into a known business expense. That solves the frustration of variable commissions eating into income, especially during high-demand weeks when drivers are working hardest.\\nDrivers are losing too much of their income to commission-based platforms and need a fairer, more predictable pricing model that lets them keep 100% of what they earn.\\\"\\n\",\"targetMarket\":\"Target market: Uber drivers, rideshare drivers, and traditional cab drivers who are tired of losing a percentage of every fare. The MVP gives them a simple alternative: pay one fixed monthly fee, keep 100% of fares, and operate with more control, predictability, and better earning potential.\\n\",\"experience\":\"Relevant experience: 20+ years in finance, accounting, forecasting, business partnering, and growth planning, plus hands-on experience building and evaluating multiple ventures across construction, transport, tourism, consulting, and tech. You also understand SME pain points, pricing models, compliance, and how to turn ideas into practical MVPs.\\n\",\"capacity\":\"5-10 hours a week whilst working on all my other projects.\\n\",\"budget\":\"Total is probably NZ$5000 max.\\n\",\"network\":\"Strong business network across New Zealand and Samoa through accounting, consulting, transport, construction, tourism, and community work. Access to SME owners, potential pilot customers, business advisers, and referral channels, plus growing links to investors, grant bodies, and strategic partners relevant to early validation.\\n\"}","metadata":{"emulator":{"name":"functions"},"function":{"name":"us-central1-pitchLabEvaluation"},"extension":{},"message":"\u001b[90m> \u001b[39m PitchLab: Raw request data: {\"idea\":\"Uber competitor business model where drivers only pay a fixed monthly fee - drivers will keep 100% of the fares earned.\\n\",\"category\":\"SaaS\",\"problem\":\"\\\"Drivers feel punished by commission-based platforms\\nOn Uber-style models, the platform takes a cut of every trip, so drivers can feel like they are doing the work while the platform keeps too much of the upside. Your model gives drivers 100% of each fare, which is much easier to understand and feels fairer.\\nDrivers want predictable costs\\nA fixed monthly subscription turns platform cost into a known business expense. That solves the frustration of variable commissions eating into income, especially during high-demand weeks when drivers are working hardest.\\nDrivers are losing too much of their income to commission-based platforms and need a fairer, more predictable pricing model that lets them keep 100% of what they earn.\\\"\\n\",\"targetMarket\":\"Target market: Uber drivers, rideshare drivers, and traditional cab drivers who are tired of losing a percentage of every fare. The MVP gives them a simple alternative: pay one fixed monthly fee, keep 100% of fares, and operate with more control, predictability, and better earning potential.\\n\",\"experience\":\"Relevant experience: 20+ years in finance, accounting, forecasting, business partnering, and growth planning, plus hands-on experience building and evaluating multiple ventures across construction, transport, tourism, consulting, and tech. You also understand SME pain points, pricing models, compliance, and how to turn ideas into practical MVPs.\\n\",\"capacity\":\"5-10 hours a week whilst working on all my other projects.\\n\",\"budget\":\"Total is probably NZ$5000 max.\\n\",\"network\":\"Strong business network across New Zealand and Samoa through accounting, consulting, transport, construction, tourism, and community work. Access to SME owners, potential pilot customers, business advisers, and referral channels, plus growing links to investors, grant bodies, and strategic partners relevant to early validation.\\n\"}"}}
