[info] >  PitchLab: Raw request data: {"idea":"Shield Smart Helmets are advanced safety helmets integrated with 4G connectivity, cameras, and real-time communication features designed for construction and civil industries. The product aims to improve worker safety, monitoring, and compliance on-site. The long-term vision is to become a standard safety platform across construction and infrastructure projects.\n","category":"Marketplace","problem":"Construction sites face ongoing safety risks, limited real-time visibility, and delayed incident reporting. Traditional PPE does not provide live monitoring or communication, reducing the ability to proactively manage hazards. There is also increasing pressure from regulators and contractors to improve safety outcomes and accountability.\n","targetMarket":"The primary market includes construction companies, civil contractors, and infrastructure projects in New Zealand and Australia. Secondary markets include mining, utilities, and industrial sectors globally. The total addressable market is large, but adoption depends heavily on regulation, budgets, and demonstrated ROI.\n","experience":"The founder has strong commercial, financial, and strategic experience, along with exposure to construction and transport industries. There is capability in sales positioning and partnership development. However, technical product development, hardware scaling, and deep industry adoption experience will need to be strengthened.\n","capacity":"Current team capacity is limited, with a small team covering technical, sales, and operations. Scaling will require additional technical support, distribution partners, and on-the-ground sales efforts. Without a focused pilot and clear traction, execution risk remains moderate to high.\n","budget":"An MVP can be deployed relatively low-cost by sourcing existing smart helmet hardware and branding it for pilot use, estimated at <$20K–$50K. A more robust product with custom features and compliance certification could require $100K–$300K. Early validation should focus on pilot trials with 2–3 contractors.\n","network":"The founder has access to construction and infrastructure networks in New Zealand and the Pacific, which is a strong advantage for pilot deployments. However, broader scaling will require partnerships with distributors, health and safety regulators, and large contractors. Building credibility through local case studies will be critical.\n"} {"user":"PitchLab: Raw request data: {\"idea\":\"Shield Smart Helmets are advanced safety helmets integrated with 4G connectivity, cameras, and real-time communication features designed for construction and civil industries. The product aims to improve worker safety, monitoring, and compliance on-site. The long-term vision is to become a standard safety platform across construction and infrastructure projects.\\n\",\"category\":\"Marketplace\",\"problem\":\"Construction sites face ongoing safety risks, limited real-time visibility, and delayed incident reporting. Traditional PPE does not provide live monitoring or communication, reducing the ability to proactively manage hazards. There is also increasing pressure from regulators and contractors to improve safety outcomes and accountability.\\n\",\"targetMarket\":\"The primary market includes construction companies, civil contractors, and infrastructure projects in New Zealand and Australia. Secondary markets include mining, utilities, and industrial sectors globally. The total addressable market is large, but adoption depends heavily on regulation, budgets, and demonstrated ROI.\\n\",\"experience\":\"The founder has strong commercial, financial, and strategic experience, along with exposure to construction and transport industries. There is capability in sales positioning and partnership development. However, technical product development, hardware scaling, and deep industry adoption experience will need to be strengthened.\\n\",\"capacity\":\"Current team capacity is limited, with a small team covering technical, sales, and operations. Scaling will require additional technical support, distribution partners, and on-the-ground sales efforts. Without a focused pilot and clear traction, execution risk remains moderate to high.\\n\",\"budget\":\"An MVP can be deployed relatively low-cost by sourcing existing smart helmet hardware and branding it for pilot use, estimated at <$20K–$50K. A more robust product with custom features and compliance certification could require $100K–$300K. Early validation should focus on pilot trials with 2–3 contractors.\\n\",\"network\":\"The founder has access to construction and infrastructure networks in New Zealand and the Pacific, which is a strong advantage for pilot deployments. However, broader scaling will require partnerships with distributors, health and safety regulators, and large contractors. Building credibility through local case studies will be critical.\\n\"}","metadata":{"emulator":{"name":"functions"},"function":{"name":"us-central1-pitchLabEvaluation"},"extension":{},"message":"\u001b[90m> \u001b[39m PitchLab: Raw request data: {\"idea\":\"Shield Smart Helmets are advanced safety helmets integrated with 4G connectivity, cameras, and real-time communication features designed for construction and civil industries. The product aims to improve worker safety, monitoring, and compliance on-site. The long-term vision is to become a standard safety platform across construction and infrastructure projects.\\n\",\"category\":\"Marketplace\",\"problem\":\"Construction sites face ongoing safety risks, limited real-time visibility, and delayed incident reporting. Traditional PPE does not provide live monitoring or communication, reducing the ability to proactively manage hazards. There is also increasing pressure from regulators and contractors to improve safety outcomes and accountability.\\n\",\"targetMarket\":\"The primary market includes construction companies, civil contractors, and infrastructure projects in New Zealand and Australia. Secondary markets include mining, utilities, and industrial sectors globally. The total addressable market is large, but adoption depends heavily on regulation, budgets, and demonstrated ROI.\\n\",\"experience\":\"The founder has strong commercial, financial, and strategic experience, along with exposure to construction and transport industries. There is capability in sales positioning and partnership development. However, technical product development, hardware scaling, and deep industry adoption experience will need to be strengthened.\\n\",\"capacity\":\"Current team capacity is limited, with a small team covering technical, sales, and operations. Scaling will require additional technical support, distribution partners, and on-the-ground sales efforts. Without a focused pilot and clear traction, execution risk remains moderate to high.\\n\",\"budget\":\"An MVP can be deployed relatively low-cost by sourcing existing smart helmet hardware and branding it for pilot use, estimated at <$20K–$50K. A more robust product with custom features and compliance certification could require $100K–$300K. Early validation should focus on pilot trials with 2–3 contractors.\\n\",\"network\":\"The founder has access to construction and infrastructure networks in New Zealand and the Pacific, which is a strong advantage for pilot deployments. However, broader scaling will require partnerships with distributors, health and safety regulators, and large contractors. Building credibility through local case studies will be critical.\\n\"}"}}
